---
/*
  This is not a layout but just a component that's used in page layouts.
  We self-host the Inter variable font (weight axis 100-900 in one file,
  latin subset) instead of pulling system fonts only, so the site renders
  identically on macOS, Windows, Linux and Android.

  Here's the formula for best font load performance.
  1. Serve from same origin as woff/woff2
  2. Load font @font-face definitions as inline styles in page <head>
  3. Preload the same origin font URLs

  Hosting providers like Netlify/Vercel automatically cache your
  public assets (fonts) and serve from their CDN closest to the users.

  Read more here to understand font load performance
  https://sia.codes/posts/making-google-fonts-faster

  Variable woff2 downloaded from Fontsource:
  https://fontsource.org/fonts/inter (latin, wght axis, normal + italic)
*/
---
<Fragment>
  <link
    rel="preload"
    href="/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-normal.woff2"
    as="font"
    type="font/woff2"
    crossorigin="crossorigin"
  />
  <link
    rel="preload"
    href="/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-italic.woff2"
    as="font"
    type="font/woff2"
    crossorigin="crossorigin"
  />
  <style is:inline>
    /* inter-variable (wght 100-900) - latin, normal */
    @font-face {
      font-family: "InterVariable";
      font-style: normal;
      font-weight: 100 900;
      font-display: fallback;
      src: local(""), url("/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-normal.woff2")
          format("woff2-variations"),
        url("/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-normal.woff2") format("woff2");
    }
    /* inter-variable (wght 100-900) - latin, italic */
    @font-face {
      font-family: "InterVariable";
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 100 900;
      font-display: fallback;
      src: local(""), url("/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-italic.woff2")
          format("woff2-variations"),
        url("/fonts/inter-variable-latin-wght-italic.woff2") format("woff2");
    }
  </style>
</Fragment>
